# Build context for deploy/Dockerfile.
#
# The image is built from Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock and src/ only. Everything else
# is documentation, deployment scaffolding, local state or build output and
# would only make the context bigger (and docker build slower).
#
# Keep Cargo.lock in the context: the image is built with `cargo build
# --release --locked`, so the lock file is part of the build inputs.
target/
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
deploy/
docs/
tests/
scripts/
README.md

# The MIT and Apache texts are copied into the image so a pulled image carries
# its own licenses; keep them in the build context.

# Local state and editor noise (also in .gitignore).
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.lock
!Cargo.lock
local-config.toml
.DS_Store
/tmp/
